    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "The short answer",
      "items": [
        "The Desk refuses a read once ten customers are read",
        "every effect it proposes goes to the gate, which escalates an email change to a person and records each verdict in the signed ledger",
        "An allowed effect reaches the MCP client, which calls surface B with no credential, and surface B adds the Lab's key"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "slate",
      "title": "Not shown here",
      "items": [
        "How the call reached the Desk, drawn by the previous question",
        "the ledger, the approval and the keys, drawn by the presenter and trust questions",
        "Connected but out of scope: gateway channel, Signed ledger, poly approve, Hello surface, Recorded MCP server, poly check and admit"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "What it guarantees",
      "items": [
        "A Desk refuses a read once it has read ten customers, and no path takes it past nineteen: The server decides how many customers a page holds, so the worst case is 9 + 10; the field's domain 0..19 states the bound and the check proves no path escapes it.",
        "An email change runs only after a person signs its approval; a phone or address change runs at once."
      ]
    }
  ]
